        model: "The Chief Experience Officer owns the neurodiverse UX principles; the design system team owns the inclusive patterns, and products may not change them on their own. User research owns the test strategy: every key journey is tested with neurodivergent people before release, with the support they need, and the results go to an owner who can stop a release. Marketing owns the brand within the calm-default rule; product teams own their journeys within the patterns. When brand, technology, product logic and inclusion conflict, the user's ability to complete a task in a stressful moment comes first, then the brand, then technical and product convenience; the management decides what that does not settle.",
